# darshana — library entry. Re-exports the three domain modules so
# consumers (smoke.cyr, tests/darshana.tcyr) can pull the whole API
# surface via a single include. `cyrius distlib` reads [lib].modules
# from cyrius.cyml directly and bundles termios/ansi/cursor into
# dist/darshana.cyr — this file is not part of the dist bundle.
#
# Public surface: the authoritative list is `scripts/smoke.sh`
# (required_syms / required_flags), enforced against dist on every CI
# run; `dist/darshana.cyr` is the shipped artifact. This comment does
# NOT re-list every symbol — that enumeration drifted pre-0.7.0 (it
# still named the now-private `tty_apply_raw_flags` and the renamed
# `tty_itoa`). Modules by concern:
#   termios.cyr  — termios raw/cooked, winsize, isatty, signalfd, TIO_*
#   ansi.cyr     — alt-screen / clear / cursor-visibility / SGR color
#   cursor.cyr   — tty_dec_buf (decimal formatter), cursor positioning
#
# Naming conventions (frozen at v1.0):
#   tty_*  public functions        tio_*  termios LE field codec
#   TIO_*  termios bit flags        TTY_*  darshana-defined constants
#   TIOC*  raw kernel ioctl nums    _*     private-by-convention
#                                          (in the bundle, not the API)
#
# Return conventions across the public surface. Every public fn falls
# in exactly one of these four buckets — the trailing "..." this block
# carried through v0.9.2 hid the fact that the unconditional emitters
# are their own bucket, which made the block false for 12 of the 29
# public fns.
#   • validating side-effecting ops — tty_raw, tty_cooked,
#     tty_winsize, tty_move, tty_sgr, tty_fg_rgb, tty_bg_rgb — 0 on
#     success, -1 on failure or out-of-range reject (rejected before
#     any byte reaches fd 1).
#   • unconditional emitters — tty_alt_enter/leave, tty_clear,
#     tty_clear_to_eol/eos, tty_cursor_hide/show/home, tty_sgr_reset,
#     tty_cursor_up/down — ALWAYS 0. The write(2) result is not
#     checked (rationale in ansi.cyr's header). `n <= 0` on
#     tty_cursor_up/down is a documented no-op, not a reject: these
#     never return -1.
#   • `_buf` composers (tty_dec_buf, tty_sgr_buf, tty_sgr_reset_buf,
#     tty_fg_rgb_buf, tty_bg_rgb_buf, tty_fg_256_buf) — the new write
#     position, or -1 on out-of-range input OR on a negative incoming
#     `pos` (v0.9.3: a -1 from an earlier link poisons the rest of the
#     chain instead of being laundered into a write below the buffer).
#     tty_dec_buf additionally clamps `val <= 0` to a single '0'.
#     Each composer documents its own byte budget; none takes a
#     capacity argument, so sizing the buffer is the caller's job.
#   • predicates / fd openers — tty_isatty returns 1/0;
#     tty_open_signalfd returns an fd (>= 0) or exactly -1, never a
#     raw -errno.

include "src/termios.cyr"
include "src/ansi.cyr"
include "src/cursor.cyr"
